<title>INDIA: India's TELCO 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's TELCO 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    7,623.6  vs    5,300.2</p>
<p>    Sales		 100,965.9  vs   78,505.8</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   8.0  vs	  6.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  87,036.9  vs   67,951.4</p>
<p>    Gross Operating    13,929.0  vs   10,554.4</p>
<p>Margin</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  2,092.4  vs    1,644.4</p>
<p>    Operating Profit   11,836.6  vs    8,910.0</p>
<p>    Other income	    318.4  vs	305.0</p>
<p>    Interest costs	2,150.4  vs    1,607.8</p>
<p>    Wealth Tax		 11.0  vs	  3.7</p>
<p>    Income Tax	    2,370.0  vs    2,303.3</p>
<p>    Investment allowance    82.5 vs	108.0</p>
<p>(utilised) reserve</p>
<p>written back</p>
<p>Note: Tata Engineering &amp; Locomotive Company (TELCO) is India's largest truckmaker.</p>
<p>The company said it was able to achieve higher profits despite a slackening in the offtake of vehicles in the domestic market in the second half due to tigher credit, drop in freight rates and the slowdown in economic growth.</p>
<p>TELCO will hold its annual general meeting on July 30.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
